---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.6 · The 70s: Song of the Elves Preparation" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-6" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.6</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The 70s: Song of the Elves Preparation</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Close the eight real Song of the Elves skill gates without eight back-to-back marathons. Short quests spend their XP before the expensive levels; Sailing, Ranged and Hunter provide changes of pace while Farming and herbs keep growing in the background.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Reach actual, unboosted 70 in all eight Song of the Elves skills; complete the useful quest chain and prepare the 2.7 elf finale."
        stats={["Actual 70 Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore", "Actual 70 Hunter, Mining, Smithing, Woodcutting", "Actual 60 Ranged; actual 67 Sailing; Mining usually 71 from the deterministic boost plan"]}
        unlocks={["Ava's accumulator; full Fairytale II; Weiss herb patch", "The Red Reef, Sacred Grove and a camphor-hulled skiff", "Dream Mentor, Defender of Varrock and Making History complete"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Read the live account, not a projected spreadsheet.</strong> Enter with the 2.5 Piety/Sins/Troubled Tortugans state. Record current XP in every skill, plus banked herbs, teaks, metal and points; train only the gap to each named stop. A level boost is used only for Making Friends, never for the eight final Song of the Elves levels.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quiet background lanes</div><h2>Keep the passive systems working; do not turn them into alarms.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Farming:</strong> Continue Chapter 1.4's tree and fruit-tree routine, occasional Fossil Island hardwoods, herb runs and accessible Farming Contracts when convenient. There is <strong>no fixed Chapter 1 Farming exit</strong>: check actual 49 before finishing Fairytale II below, then <strong>actual 70 before this chapter's exit</strong> for Song of the Elves. Use a bounded active catch-up only for a measured shortfall. Add the disease-free Weiss herb patch after Making Friends. <strong>Birdhouses:</strong> do them when convenient, but no specific run or XP amount is assumed for Hunter. <strong>Managing Miscellania:</strong> keep the treasury funded and approval reasonable. Stay herb-heavy; put the other workers on teaks while Construction still needs planks, then move them to maples for nests/seeds or coal for Smithing according to your bank. There is no daily-collection requirement.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Close old quest threads</div><h2>Three short stories, with real XP and future dependency payoff.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-icthlarin" number="1" title="Complete Icthlarin's Little Helper; record Agility">
        <p>Take a cat or kitten from Gertrude's Cat, food, combat gear and desert access via Shantay Pass. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one bucket of sap, one willow log, one bag of salt, a <strong>full waterskin(4)</strong>, tinderbox and at least 600 coins; take extra waterskins for travel so the hand-in one stays full. The Wanderer west of the Agility Pyramid, north of Sophanem draws you into hypnotised pyramid passages, then Sophanem's priest and carpenter send you through the burial preparations. The pyramid has traps and combat; bank between phases if needed and use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Icthlarin%27s_Little_Helper" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest map</a> for the hypnotised sequence. Completion opens <strong>Sophanem and its carpet connection</strong> and gives <strong>4,500 Thieving, 4,000 Agility and 4,000 Woodcutting XP</strong>. Record actual Agility now.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace the burial supplies before the desert trip">
          <p>Check the live bank even if Chapter 1 once collected sap. Use a <strong>knife on an evergreen tree with an empty bucket</strong> to collect another bucket of sap; the evergreens outside Falador work. Cut a willow log at Draynor, buy <strong>one bag of salt from a Slayer master</strong>, and buy full waterskins/desert clothing at Shantay Pass. A knife spawns in Lumbridge Castle's kitchen, and its general store supplies a bucket and tinderbox.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>linen from Raetul in eastern Sophanem for 30 coins</strong> when the burial preparation needs it. The 600-coin travel/payment buffer covers this; linen is a quest purchase, not ordinary cloth or silk. Bring your living cat/kitten; if missing, buy another kitten from Gertrude for 100 coins. Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer and antipoison recovery</a> if the bank has no doses.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-tail" number="2" title="Complete A Tail of Two Cats; use both lamps on Herblore">
        <p>With your cat and catspeak amulet, start at <strong>Unferth in east Burthorpe</strong>. Hild can enchant the amulet for five death runes: its whiskers then work like a compass to locate roaming Bob. His exact position changes, so use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Tail_of_Two_Cats" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current Bob-location guide</a> rather than a fixed coordinate. <strong>Bank check:</strong> five death runes, one whole chocolate cake, one ordinary log, tinderbox, bucket of milk, shears, <strong>four potato seeds</strong>, rake, seed dibber, vial of water, desert shirt and desert robe. The potato patch grows while you do the other parts. The quest closes direct future <strong>While Guthix Sleeps</strong> and <strong>Dragon Slayer II</strong> prerequisites without a new skill grind. Put <strong>both 2,500-XP lamps into Herblore</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare Unferth's actual chore kit">
          <p>At <strong>50 Cooking</strong>, use a chocolate bar on a <strong>whole cake</strong> to make the chocolate cake. Steal the cake from an Ardougne cake stall and buy the chocolate bar and milk from the Culinaromancer's Chest; a part-eaten cake is not the hand-in. Buy the five death runes from Aubury.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>four potato seeds from Olivia in Draynor</strong>, and missing rake/dibber from Sarah's Farming shop south of Falador. Shantay sells the <strong>desert shirt and desert robe</strong>; take the actual two clothing pieces, not generic desert protection. Jatix supplies the vial of water. Cut the log and replace shears/tinderbox at Lumbridge's general store.</p>
          <p>If the <strong>catspeak amulet</strong> was lost, ask the <strong>Sphinx in Sophanem</strong> for another; recover a kitten from Gertrude if needed. The quest provides the doctor/nurse hat during its disguise sequence, so there is no outside hat purchase.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-fairytale" number="3" title="Finish Fairytale II; put its lamp into Herblore">
        <p>Chapter 1 deliberately stopped after fairy rings unlocked. Now check <strong>actual 40 Thieving, 49 Farming and 57 Herblore</strong>. If passive Farming is still below 49, continue the available tree/fruit-tree circuit or use a short, chosen Tithe bridge for only the live gap; <strong>do not mark this quest complete until actual 49</strong>. Then finish the partial quest rather than treating this as a new ring unlock. Carry a dramen/lunar staff, vial of water, pestle and mortar, food and a suitable weapon. Follow Nuff's certificate/ring sequence, recover the Queen's secateurs, then gather star flower and a Gorak claw for the magic essence potion. <strong>Goraks ignore protection prayers</strong>; bring food and consider safespotting rather than relying on Prayer. Full completion gives <strong>3,500 Herblore XP</strong> and a selectable <strong>2,500-XP lamp for Herblore</strong>, and lets later POH fairy-ring content rely on the full quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fairytale_II_-_Cure_a_Queen" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the certificate and make this quest's own potion">
          <p>Search <strong>Fairy Nuff's room in north-west Zanaris</strong> for another Nuff's certificate if it is no longer banked, and read it before repeating the ring-code sequence. A missing dramen staff can be remade with the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-lunar`}>Lunar preparation's Entrana method</a>; buy a vial of water and pestle and mortar from Jatix.</p>
          <p>The potion ingredients are <strong>quest-local</strong>: pick a star flower on the <strong>CKP</strong> plane when it grows, and obtain a claw from a Gorak on <strong>DIR</strong>. At 57 Herblore, put the star flower in the vial of water and add the claw crushed with the pestle and mortar. This is <strong>magic essence</strong>, not a potion made from the ordinary herb stock.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged · first half</div><h2>Claim the easy upgrade and quest lamp before the longer 60 gate.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-ranged-50" number="4" title="Reach actual 50 Ranged, then pause">
        <p>Mourning's End Part I eventually needs <strong>actual 60 Ranged</strong>, but do not do the whole gap at once. Check live level after earlier quest rewards; train only to <strong>actual 50</strong>. Gemstone Crab in the Tlati Rainforest is a relaxed, long-idle target; Ammonite or Sand Crabs work too. For cheap Ironman ammo, buy a <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow and bone bolts from Nardok in the Dorgesh-Kaan mine</strong>, accessible after The Lost Tribe; the shop stocks the crossbow and inexpensive bolts/packs. Use the earlier arrow stock instead if preferred. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nardok%27s_Bone_Weapons" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Shop stock</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-ranged-methods" informational={true} skill="Ranged" target="actual 50 now, 60 later" why="Split the unboostable elf-quest gate and spend Dream Mentor's lamp before the second half." recommended="Gemstone Crab or another low-attention crab with cheap bone bolts." relaxed="Use existing arrows with Ava's attractor if the stock is already convenient." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-accumulator" number="5" title="Upgrade Ava's attractor to accumulator">
        <p>At <strong>actual 50 Ranged</strong>, return to Ava in Draynor Manor with the <strong>existing attractor and <em>75 steel arrows actually present now</em></strong>. Upgrade to <strong>Ava's accumulator</strong>; use the retained device when it is still banked. Equip it for the remaining Ranged work. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ava%27s_accumulator" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Upgrade requirements</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the device and missing arrows">
          <p>If the arrows were used, buy the shortfall from <strong>Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock</strong>. If the attractor itself is missing, bring <strong>999 coins plus 75 steel arrows</strong> to Ava for the accumulator at actual 50 Ranged. The retained attractor replaces the 999-coin payment when you still have it.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-dream" number="6" title="Complete Dream Mentor; put the dreamy lamp into Ranged">
        <p>Check Lunar Diplomacy, Eadgar's Ruse and actual 85+ combat; check the current goutweed stock. Start with <strong>Cyrisus in the Lunar Isle mine</strong>; <strong>bank check:</strong> seal of passage, <strong>20 pieces of food in three types (7 + 7 + 6)</strong> for Cyrisus, one goutweed, one astral rune, hammer, pestle and mortar, and <strong>tinderbox</strong>. The quest supplies its special dream vial. Rebank into your strongest reliable combat gear and <strong>many high-healing food pieces</strong> before the dream: there are <strong>four consecutive bosses, no Prayer and no emergency teleport</strong>. The dream lectern is the exit if you need to restart. Read each boss's mechanics first; do not assume Piety carries the encounter. Rewards are <strong>15,000 Hitpoints and 10,000 Magic XP</strong> plus a <strong>15,000-XP dreamy lamp</strong> for a combat skill other than Attack or Prayer. Put that lamp into <strong>Ranged</strong>. This also closes a While Guthix Sleeps prerequisite. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dream_Mentor" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boss guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Separate Cyrisus's food from the boss inventory">
          <p>Cyrisus needs three distinct food types. For a simple refill, catch/cook <strong>seven salmon, seven tuna and six lobsters</strong>: fly-fish salmon at Lumbridge/Shilo and fish the sea types at Catherby with a harpoon and lobster pot from Gerrant. Cook until the required <em>successful</em> counts are banked. Use other suitable banked food types if you already have them; keep your high-healing boss food separate.</p>
          <p>If Eadgar's Ruse used the last <strong>goutweed</strong>, steal another from the <strong>Troll Stronghold kitchen storeroom</strong> using its guard-avoidance route. This is not a gout tuber. Buy the astral rune from <strong>Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle</strong>, and ask Brundt in Rellekka for a replacement seal of passage. Fill the <strong>quest-provided dream vial</strong> and follow the goutweed/ground-astral sequence; an ordinary shop vial does not replace it.</p>
          <p>Before entering the dream, refill high-healing food with the established Tai Bwo Wannai karambwan fishing/cooking loop. There is no prayer-potion requirement for the dream itself because Prayer is disabled; the four-boss food supply must survive that sequence.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Making Friends · spend the rewards early</div><h2>Two deterministic boosts buy a large reduction in later skilling.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-agility-65" number="7" title="Reach actual 65 Agility; make an Agility potion">
        <p>Read the post-Icthlarin level. At the <strong>Colossal Wyrm Remains in Varlamore's Avium Savannah</strong>, continue the basic course until <strong>actual 62</strong>, then use its advanced course through <strong>actual 65</strong>. The August 2026 longer-lap update reduced inputs while scaling rewards, making it a good lower-input default; Seers rooftops are an alternative <strong>once actual 60 is reached</strong>; use Falador rooftops before that if you prefer them. Hallowed Sepulchre, unlocked by Sins, is a more active option, not an assumed method. <strong>Count live Agility-potion doses:</strong> use the four-dose bottle reserved during Tai Bwo Wannai Trio preparation if it remains, or refill the shortfall through 2.4's <strong>Brimhaven Agility Arena toadflax</strong> (three vouchers per herb), vial of water and <strong>Gnome Stronghold swamp toad's legs</strong> recipe. A banked or farmed toadflax is fine, but the variable Master Farmer/patch branch is not the required supplier. Do not count Trio's consumed bottle again. The potion gives <strong>+3 Agility</strong>, so <strong>65 + 3 = 68</strong> for Making Friends. No Summer pie is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Colossal_agility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Course details</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-agility-methods" informational={true} skill="Agility" target="actual 65 for the quest, then 70 later" why="The +3 potion reaches the boostable 68 check; Making Friends then awards 50,000 Agility XP." recommended="Basic-to-advanced Colossal Wyrm course at 62, then continue to 65." relaxed="Seers rooftops if you prefer marks of grace." fast="Hallowed Sepulchre if you enjoy a more active obstacle run." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-eagles" number="8" title="Complete Eagles' Peak as a quest break">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Charlie at Ardougne Zoo</strong> and follow the eagle-rescue trail to the Piscatoris area. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one yellow dye, one swamp tar and 50 coins, plus food and a teleport. Collect the quest's feathers and puzzle items locally. The quest awards <strong>2,500 Hunter XP</strong>, unlocks <strong>box traps</strong> and enables chinchompa hunting—long-term options, not a mandatory chin grind. This short quest breaks up the two Making Friends skill preparations. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Eagles%27_Peak" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supply the beak/cape ingredients">
          <p>Make <strong>yellow dye at Aggie in Draynor with two onions and five coins</strong>, or use one still banked. Pick up one swamp tar in Lumbridge Swamp. During the quest collect <strong>ten eagle feathers</strong> in the Eagles' Peak caves; take these, the dye, tar and 50 coins to <strong>Azyff in Varrock's Fancy Clothes Store</strong> for two fake beaks and two eagle capes.</p>
          <p>The metal feather, coloured puzzle feathers, odd bird seed and ferret-catching equipment are supplied in the quest area. The first completion does not require a pre-purchased rope or a stock of Hunter bait.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-mining-71" number="9" title="Reach actual 71 Mining; buy a dwarven stout">
        <p>From the actual-60 Lunar checkpoint, train only the live gap to <strong>actual 71</strong>. Shooting Stars are the relaxed option; Motherlode Mine is the resource-focused option because its ores can feed Smithing. A normal <strong>dwarven stout gives +1 Mining</strong> and can be bought from <strong>the Rising Sun Inn in Falador</strong>; <strong>71 + 1 = 72</strong> at the Making Friends check. This also clears Song of the Elves' unboosted 70 Mining gate. If you strongly prefer avoiding level 71 and accept RNG, actual 70 plus a successful +2 orange-spice stew is optional; it is <em>not</em> this route's default. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Temporary_skill_boost" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boost reference</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-mining-methods" informational={true} skill="Mining" target="actual 71" why="A cheap +1 stout reaches Making Friends' boostable 72 gate without stew RNG." recommended="Shooting Stars for lower attention; finish only the live remainder." resource="Motherlode Mine when you want ores for the later Smithing work." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-friends" number="10" title="Complete Making Friends with My Arm; open Weiss">
        <p>Confirm <strong>actual 66 Firemaking</strong> (already exceeded), <strong>35 Construction</strong> (exceeded), and completed <strong>Swan Song, Cold War, My Arm's Big Adventure and Romeo &amp; Juliet</strong> (the last was finished in 1.1). Use the <strong>four-dose Agility potion reserved in 2.4</strong> and bring access to extra <strong>dwarven stouts</strong>; reapply the <strong>65→68 Agility</strong> and <strong>71→72 Mining</strong> boosts when the relevant checks occur. If that potion was spent, repeat 2.4's Brimhaven Arena toadflax + toad's-legs recipe for only the missing doses. Bank-audit the story supplies: <strong>saw, hammer, one bolt of cloth, five mahogany planks and one cadava berry</strong>. If the berry was not banked after Romeo &amp; Juliet, pick one from the <strong>wild cadava bushes directly west of the south-east Varrock mine</strong> before visiting the Varrock Apothecary. Bring combat gear, food, Prayer restores, tinderbox and troll-area travel. A <strong>bucket of water, rope and pickaxe</strong> are also required, but can be obtained during the quest; bring your own to avoid detours. Bank before the fight and follow the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_Friends_with_My_Arm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current quest/boss guide</a> for the fire-pit and monster mechanics. Claim <strong>50,000 Agility, 50,000 Mining, 40,000 Firemaking and 10,000 Construction XP</strong>. The <strong>disease-free Weiss herb patch</strong> joins your normal herb runs now. Record actual Agility, Mining and Construction; do not infer levels from the rewards.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Buy new cloth and planks; refill both temporary boosts">
          <p>Buy the <strong>bolt of cloth for 650 coins from the Varrock sawmill operator</strong>. Check for <strong>five mahogany planks still present</strong> after the lectern and Cold War; if short, cut the missing mahogany logs north of the Farming Guild and convert them at a sawmill for <strong>1,500 coins each</strong>. The full five cost 7,500 coins in conversion fees.</p>
          <p>Buy ordinary <strong>dwarven stouts from the Rising Sun Inn in Falador</strong> for the +1 Mining check. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-trio`}>Trio preparation</a> gives the repeatable toadflax/toad's-legs recipe for the <strong>Agility potion(4)</strong>. Carry enough doses/drinks to repeat checks if a boost expires; the previously reserved potion is not guaranteed to survive earlier use.</p>
          <p>Replace hammer/tinderbox/bucket at Lumbridge's general store, saw at the sawmill, rope from Ned, and pickaxe from Nurmof in the Dwarven Mine if needed. Refill combat supplies through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion supply note</a> before the fight.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Sailing · first return</div><h2>A quest at 52 makes the trip more than a level bar.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-52" number="11" title="Sail from the live post-Tortugans level to actual 52">
        <p>After Troubled Tortugans, use <strong>The Summer Shore notice board</strong> for courier tasks: accept a delivery, pick up the crate at its ledger, put it in your cargo hold, sail to the destination and deposit it at the receiving ledger. Choose available routes rather than forcing one perfect loop. Chart newly reachable water/landmarks for one-time XP and salvage when you want a different texture. Bring routine food/repair supplies where your route crosses danger. Stop at <strong>actual 52 Sailing</strong>; do not count Troubled Tortugans' 10,000 XP twice. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sailing_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current training guide</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-reef" number="12" title="Complete The Red Reef; bank its Sailing and Smithing XP">
        <p>Check <strong>actual 52 Sailing and 48 Smithing</strong>, plus Troubled Tortugans. Begin with the Tortugans at <strong>The Summer Shore/Great Conch</strong>. Preflight the boat with working cannons and ammunition <em>or</em> suitable Magic/Ranged gear to attack the pirate crews; bring <strong>repair kits covering at least roughly 300 boat hitpoints</strong>, food, protection-prayer supplies and land-combat gear. The quest includes two hostile pirate boats, pirates on land and later bosses. <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> helps against ship captains, and bank/regear before the island fights. Boat <em>capsizing</em> is not a Hardcore death, but your character reaching zero Hitpoints aboard or on an island is an unsafe death; HCIM should not treat this as a harmless minigame. Read the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Red_Reef" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest combat guide</a> before the instanced fight. Claim <strong>15,000 Sailing and 5,000 Smithing XP</strong>, <strong>Sacred Grove/camphor resources</strong> and the <strong>Bosun's Bench schematic</strong>. Record Smithing before planning 55 or 70.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Refill repair kits and combat supplies before sailing out">
          <p>The Magic/Ranged crew-kill route avoids needing a cannon upgrade or cannonball stock. Use the combat equipment you already own. The quest supplies the <strong>deep sea helmet and apparatus</strong> for its dive; these are not the earlier RFD diving items.</p>
          <p>For the roughly 300-boat-HP reserve, make <strong>ten mahogany repair kits</strong> (30 repair each) at a <strong>shipwright's workbench</strong>, using its mahogany-kit recipe; your actual 62+ Construction clears the 47 requirement. Bring hammer and saw. Refill the recipe's <strong>mahogany planks</strong> by cutting logs north of the Farming Guild and paying a sawmill 1,500 coins each; make <strong>mithril nails</strong> at an anvil from mithril bars (Ordan's mithril ore plus four coal per bar), and buy <strong>swamp paste from Shipwright Seb or the Port Khazard general store</strong>. Make only the live kit shortfall, checking the workbench's required quantities before buying a batch.</p>
          <p>Repair kits heal the boat, not your character. Bank fresh food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer potions</a> for the land fights as a separate supply check.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Hunter and Smithing · useful interim stops</div><h2>Let Defender's rewards reduce both later grinds.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i26-hunter-52" number="13" title="Reach actual 52 Hunter with live birdhouse XP counted">
        <p>Check the skill tab after Eagles' Peak and any birdhouses. For a deterministic catch-up, travel to the <strong>Hunter Guild in Varlamore</strong> and speak to <strong>Guild Scribe Verity in the Burrow</strong>. At actual 46, Huntmaster Gilman gives <strong>Novice Hunters' Rumours</strong>: receive an assigned creature, bring the normal trap/tools for it, hunt until its rare part appears, then return it for Hunter XP and a loot sack. Assignments and rare-part timing vary; consult the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hunters%27_Rumours" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">creature/trap reference</a> as needed, with no block-list meta required. No particular task or number of birdhouses is assumed. Stop temporarily at <strong>actual 52</strong> for Defender.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-smithing-55" number="14" title="Reach actual 55 Smithing, not 70 yet">
        <p>Count the <strong>5,000 Smithing XP from The Red Reef</strong> and check live XP. Use <strong>Giants' Foundry</strong> for the resource-efficient default: bring banked metal bars to the foundry south of Al Kharid, cast a sword in the mould, then work its heat/shape stations as the progress markers direct. Use banked-bar smithing for a simpler anvil loop, or Blast Furnace gold with the Family Crest <strong>goldsmith gauntlets</strong> if you want a faster active alternative and have ore. Stop at <strong>actual 55</strong>; Defender then gives 15,000 more XP. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giants%27_Foundry" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Foundry primer</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-smithing-methods" informational={true} skill="Smithing" target="actual 55 now, 70 after Defender" why="Spend the quest's 15,000 XP before paying for the final stretch." recommended="Giants' Foundry from available metal bars." relaxed="Ordinary bar smithing at an anvil." fast="Blast Furnace gold with goldsmith gauntlets if you have the resources." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-rc-35" number="15" title="Verify actual 35 Runecraft; no new grind is expected">
        <p>The named, mandatory rewards alone are <strong>1,000 Enter the Abyss + 6,000 The Eyes of Glouphrie + 500 The Ascent of Arceuus + 5,000 Lunar Diplomacy + 9,210 Temple of the Eye + 3,500 The Slug Menace = 25,210 Runecraft XP</strong>, even ignoring all starting/training XP. Level 35 starts at <strong>22,406 XP</strong> and level 36 at <strong>24,742 XP</strong>, so the route actually guarantees <strong>at least actual 36</strong> before What Lies Below's 35 gate. Verify that each quest reward was claimed and read the skill tab. If a named quest is somehow incomplete, finish/claim it first; if the actual account still shows below 35, use only the visible remainder via a few Guardians of the Rift rounds. This is a dependency check, not an automatic grind.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-what" number="16" title="Complete What Lies Below">
        <p>With <strong>actual 35 Runecraft</strong>, speak to <strong>Rat Burgiss south of Varrock</strong>. Bring a chaos talisman/tiara or use the <strong>Temple of the Eye's Guardian of Chaos</strong> route to the chaos altar; the latter avoids a Wilderness trip. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one <strong>empty bowl</strong> and <strong>15 chaos runes</strong>, plus Varrock travel, food and combat gear. Follow Surok's investigation and the King Roald encounter using the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/What_Lies_Below" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>. Claim <strong>8,000 Runecraft XP</strong>. This quest is the final newly supplied Defender prerequisite.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Bring the hand-ins and use a supplied altar route">
          <p>Buy <strong>15 chaos runes from Aubury</strong>. Make an empty bowl from one soft clay at the <strong>Rimmington pottery wheel, then fire it in the pottery oven</strong> (8 Crafting); this is a fired bowl, unlike Dragon Slayer's unfired one. Rat and Surok provide the folder, letters and metal wand during their steps.</p>
          <p>At <strong>35 Runecraft</strong>, enter a Guardians of the Rift game and use the active <strong>Guardian of Chaos</strong> portal when it appears. Take Surok's wand and all 15 chaos runes to the altar and charge the wand there. Temple of the Eye is complete, so this route needs no chaos talisman or new Wilderness access; no extra rune essence is needed for the wand charge.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-defender" number="17" title="Complete Defender of Varrock; claim its museum lamp">
        <p>Check <strong>actual 55 Smithing and 52 Hunter</strong>. The quest log already contains <strong>Shield of Arrav, Temple of Ikov, Below Ice Mountain, Family Crest, Garden of Tranquillity (and Creature of Fenkenstrain), What Lies Below, Romeo &amp; Juliet, Demon Slayer and Rune Mysteries</strong>. Start with <strong>Elias White at the Jolly Boar Inn</strong>. Take a pickaxe for barronite, teleport options for Varrock/Camdozaal, food, prayer supplies and the retained <strong>Salve amulet</strong> for armoured zombies; the route's Piety/defender kit exceeds the combat recommendation. Follow the tracks, forge work and Varrock defence in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Defender_of_Varrock" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>. Claim <strong>15,000 Smithing and 15,000 Hunter XP</strong> and access to <strong>Zemouregal's Base</strong>. At the Varrock Museum, talk to <strong>Historian Minas</strong> for the separate <strong>5,000-XP antique lamp</strong>; put it into <strong>Herblore</strong>. This helps three current 70 grinds and prepares While Guthix Sleeps.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Collect the forge ingredients in Camdozaal">
          <p>No outside bar, ore or gem hand-in is required. The quest supplies its mist bottle and other story items. In <strong>Camdozaal</strong>, mine the required <strong>barronite deposit</strong> and fight a <strong>chaos golem for a chaos core</strong> when instructed, then use the quest's forge process. Bring a pickaxe you actually own; Nurmof in the Dwarven Mine sells replacements.</p>
          <p>The retained Salve is recommended combat equipment. If it is missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-5/#i25-haunted`}>Haunted Mine preparation</a> to replace the crystal and wool, then Tarn's diary for its enchantment. Refill food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer doses</a> before the zombie fights.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Chapter 3 boundary:</strong> Path of Glouphrie would add an otherwise unnecessary <strong>actual 56 Slayer</strong> grind, so Chapter 3 must supply it before While Guthix Sleeps. The Curse of Arrav and Mage Arena II are also deferred; neither raises a Song of the Elves skill. Do not train Ranged to 62 or Magic to 75 just for them here.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Construction, then a Sailing break</div><h2>Use the plank sack and the live bank, not a fixed contract quota.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-construction-70" number="18" title="Train Construction to actual 70">
        <p>Count the actual 2.1 endpoint (at least 62), <strong>Darkness of Hallowvale's 2,000 Construction XP</strong>, <strong>Making Friends' 10,000 XP</strong>, and any real contract/shipbuilding XP. Use the plank sack and <strong>Adept Mahogany Homes</strong> with kingdom teaks and remaining 2.1 planks first. If neither is stocked, repeat <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-1/#i21-teak-prep`}>2.1's ordinary teak-cutting and sawmill loop</a>; the Castle Wars tree works when Fossil Island trees are unavailable. Refill steel bars from Ordan's iron ore and coal, so kingdom collection timing cannot block actual 70. From the conservative actual-62 floor, the two named quest rewards leave roughly <strong>390,000 XP</strong> to level 70; at an average around <strong>280 total XP per teak plank</strong> in Adept contracts, roughly <strong>1,400 teaks</strong> is a planning scale, not an exact bill. Starting above 62, varying contracts and banked planks move this substantially: think <strong>roughly 1,000–1,500 teaks total</strong> from the conservative start, and prepare/top up in smaller batches rather than chopping a rigid total. Faster POH furniture uses more planks but remains a choice. Once the remaining plank need is comfortably covered, non-herb kingdom workers can switch to maples or coal. Stop at <strong>actual, unboosted 70</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mahogany_Homes" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Contract reference</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-construction-methods" informational={true} skill="Construction" target="actual 70" why="Song of the Elves needs an unboosted 70; the plank budget depends on the real 2.1 exit level." recommended="Adept Mahogany Homes, plank sack, kingdom teaks and live-level checks." fast="POH furniture if you value speed over teak efficiency." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-60" number="19" title="Return to Sailing; pause at actual 60">
        <p>Count The Red Reef's <strong>15,000 Sailing XP</strong> and sail from the observed level. Rotate ordinary Summer Shore courier deliveries with new charting and salvage rather than repeating one loop until 67. Stop at <strong>actual 60</strong>: camphor-era ship facilities begin to matter around here, and this is a useful pacing break, <em>not</em> a Song of the Elves gate. Keep any camphor gathered in the Sacred Grove for later ship work.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged and Hunter · second half</div><h2>Return to the earlier lanes with quest XP already banked.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-ranged-60" number="20" title="Finish actual 60 Ranged for Mourning's End Part I">
        <p>Count earlier Ranged quests, the Dream Mentor <strong>15,000-XP lamp</strong> and actual training; read live XP. With the accumulator equipped, return to Gemstone/Ammonite/Sand Crabs and train only the remaining gap to <strong>actual, unboosted 60</strong>. The cheap Ironman default is Nardok's <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow plus bone bolts</strong>; buy bolts/packs in manageable batches as the stack runs down. Existing bows/arrows are fine. Stop at 60, not 62 for the deferred Curse of Arrav.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-hunter-70" number="21" title="Finish actual 70 Hunter with rumours as the catch-up">
        <p>Read live Hunter after Eagles' Peak's <strong>2,500</strong>, Defender's <strong>15,000</strong> and whatever birdhouse XP actually happened. Continue the Hunter Guild loop. At <strong>actual 57</strong>, ask Cervus or Ornus for <strong>Adept rumours</strong>; they use the same assigned-creature → rare-part → return loop but a different task pool and better loot sacks. You may keep a comfortable Novice task if preferred. Birdhouses remain a convenient background lane, never a required number of runs. No chinchompa mega-grind or task block list is assumed. Stop at <strong>actual, unboosted 70</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hunters%27_Rumours" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Rumour tiers</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">A mandatory story break</div><h2>Close Song of the Elves' easily forgotten quest prerequisite.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-making-history" number="22" title="Complete Making History and claim the museum lamp">
        <p>Start with <strong>Jorral at the outpost north-west of West Ardougne</strong>. Stage a <strong>spade, <em>unenchanted</em> strung sapphire amulet and ghostspeak amulet</strong>, plus the Ectophial, Rellekka/Ardougne travel and teleports. Ghosts Ahoy already gives free Port Phasmatys entry; no new token payment is assumed. Follow the three witness stories and enchanted-key clues in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_History" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>; there is no combat boss. Keep the <strong>enchanted key</strong> if you want its later treasure trail. Completion is a <strong>direct Song of the Elves prerequisite</strong>. Tell <strong>Historian Minas at the Varrock Museum</strong> the history for the separate <strong>1,000-XP lamp</strong> and put it into <strong>Herblore</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make the correct amulet instead of enchanting it">
          <p>At <strong>24 Crafting</strong>, use <strong>one gold bar, one cut sapphire and an amulet mould</strong> at a furnace, then add a <strong>ball of wool</strong>. Hand in this <strong>strung sapphire amulet without enchanting it</strong>; an amulet of magic is not the requested item.</p>
          <p>For a missing bar buy gold ore from Ordan and smelt it; mine/cut a sapphire at Shilo until you have one. Buy the mould from Dommik in Al Kharid and shear/spin wool at Lumbridge, or buy a ball from Aemad in East Ardougne. Father Urhney replaces a ghostspeak amulet, and a spade spawns at the Falador estate agent.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-agility-70" number="23" title="Finish actual 70 Agility after the quest rewards">
        <p>Count Icthlarin's <strong>4,000 XP</strong>, training to actual 65 and Making Friends' <strong>50,000 XP</strong>; check the skill tab. Continue the <strong>advanced Colossal Wyrm course</strong> as the lower-input default. Hallowed Sepulchre is an active alternative now that Sins is complete; neither its higher floors nor 72/77/84/98 Agility are mandatory. Stop at <strong>actual, unboosted 70</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-63" number="24" title="Sail to actual 63; decide whether to build the Bosun's Bench">
        <p>Another short courier/charting/salvage return reaches <strong>actual 63 Sailing</strong>. With <strong>54 Construction</strong> already exceeded and the Red Reef schematic unlocked, the <strong>Bosun's workbench</strong> becomes available. Its current live recipe is <strong>6 camphor planks, 24 adamantite nails and 5 lead bars</strong>, with a saw/hammer and the quest schematic. A crewmate assigned to it uses repair kits from the cargo hold to repair the boat automatically. You may wait until the deterministic adamantite-nail preparation after Smithing 70 below; do not grind rare salvage just to build it at 63. Build it only if you expect enough ship combat to value the automation; <strong>ownership is optional</strong> and creates no progress checkbox. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bosun%27s_workbench" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Facility recipe</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Finish the material-heavy gates</div><h2>Measure the bank and XP; work in batches between the remaining Sailing trips.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-smithing-70" number="25" title="Finish actual 70 Smithing">
        <p>Check actual Smithing after the 55 checkpoint, Red Reef's <strong>5,000</strong> and Defender's <strong>15,000 XP</strong> (do not double-count Reef if it was already included before 55). From exactly level 55 <em>before</em> Defender, its reward alone leaves about <strong>560,000 XP</strong> to level 70; higher starting XP and real bar work lower that. At Giants' Foundry, sword XP varies with alloy and performance, so budget against the <strong>live XP gap and banked bars</strong>, not a promised number of MLM inventories. Process ore from Motherlode Mine or other banked sources into bars; refill with ores/metal equipment only as needed. Ordinary anvil smithing is simpler; Blast Furnace gold plus goldsmith gauntlets is a faster, more active alternative if gold ore is available. Stop at <strong>actual, unboosted 70</strong>, not BRUHsailer's 74.</p>
        <p><strong>Do not miss the ship-nail dependency:</strong> the skiff hull needs <strong>300 adamantite nails</strong>, normally smithed at 74. At actual 70, buy <strong>two or three Kovac's grogs</strong> from the Giants' Foundry reward shop (<strong>300 reputation each</strong>; do a few commissions if you trained by another method). Each gives a deterministic <strong>+4 Smithing</strong>; use the boost at an anvil to turn <strong>20 adamantite bars into 300 nails</strong> (15 per bar), redrinking before it decays. Smelt the bars at actual 70 from <strong>20 adamantite ores and 120 coal</strong> or use bars already banked. If you also want the optional workbench, budget <strong>two extra bars for 30 more nails</strong>; it uses 24. No level-74 grind, spicy stew, rare salvage or player trading is assumed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Kovac%27s_grog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Grog boost</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-smithing-final-methods" informational={true} skill="Smithing" target="actual 70" why="Song of the Elves consumes 70; neither 74 nor a fixed metal inventory is required." recommended="Giants' Foundry with the bars your account actually owns." relaxed="Ordinary smithing of banked bars." fast="Blast Furnace gold with goldsmith gauntlets if resources permit." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-67" number="26" title="Sail to actual 67 and fit a camphor hull to the skiff">
        <p>Resume from actual 63 with couriers, charting and salvage, checking live XP between sessions. Stop at <strong>actual 67 Sailing</strong>: this is a Chapter 3 ship-tier handoff, not a Song of the Elves skill. The current <a href="https://umkyzn.github.io/BRUHsailer/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BRUHsailer Chapter 3 boat plan</a> <strong>uses a camphor-hulled skiff</strong>, so build that version here rather than funding a sloop hull. <strong>Check your boat first:</strong> the skiff purchase in 2.3 was optional, so if you are still using a raft, buy a <strong>skiff from a shipwright for 15,000 coins</strong> now; count the fee in the live cash check instead of assuming the optional upgrade occurred. Cut <strong>50 camphor logs</strong> in the Red Reef's Sacred Grove and turn them into <strong>50 planks at a sawmill (2,500 coins per plank)</strong>. At a shipwright's workbench, make <strong>10 camphor hull parts</strong> (five planks per part); at the shipyard fit them to your <strong>skiff</strong> with the <strong>300 adamantite nails prepared above, 20 swamp tar and 5 lead bars</strong>. Collect any missing <strong>swamp tar from the ground in Lumbridge Swamp</strong>. If you have no lead banked, mine <strong>10 lead ores in Pandemonium Cave</strong> and smelt two ores per bar at a furnace; the 25 Mining/Smithing checks are already cleared. The hull requires <strong>67 Sailing and 59 Construction</strong>, both cleared. Check existing supplies before gathering; a sloop would require 16 large parts/roughly 400 camphor planks and is <em>not</em> imposed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Camphor_hull" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boat-specific recipes</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-herblore-70" number="27" title="Finish actual 70 Herblore from the live herb bank">
        <p>Before any potion batch, count 2.5's named rewards, <strong>Sins' 90,000 XP</strong>, Tail's <strong>5,000</strong>, Fairytale II's <strong>3,500 + 2,500</strong>, Defender's museum <strong>5,000</strong>, Making History's <strong>1,000</strong>, plus every real potion's XP. From a bare actual-60 floor before Sins, those 2.6 rewards plus the tome provide <strong>107,000 guaranteed XP</strong>, leaving roughly <strong>357,000 XP</strong> to level 70 before ordinary potion XP; actual starting XP can be higher. The bank's herb/secondary quantity is <em>not</em> guaranteed. Make useful normal potions from accumulated kingdom and herb-run supplies as the lower-attention default, topping up with more runs/contracts while doing other route work if needed. Stop at <strong>actual, unboosted 70</strong>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-herblore-methods" informational={true} skill="Herblore" target="actual 70" why="A real SotE gate; herbs are the variable bottleneck, so check XP and supplies in batches." recommended="Make potions the account will use from banked herbs and secondaries." resource="Mastering Mixology converts herbs to more XP per herb without ordinary secondaries, at higher attention." />
        <ExpandableNote label="Active, resource-efficient alternative" title="Mastering Mixology in Aldarin">
          <p>With <strong>actual 60 Herblore and Children of the Sun</strong> already complete, travel to <strong>Aldarin in Varlamore</strong> and enter the Alchemical Society's lab. Refine clean herbs or unfinished potions into <strong>Mox, Aga and Lye paste</strong>, load the hopper, mix the displayed ingredient combinations, process each potion at its indicated station, and hand in the requested orders for Herblore XP and resin. It extracts more XP per herb and avoids the normal potion secondaries, but is a more active loop than ordinary potion-making. Different herbs produce different paste; check the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mastering_Mixology" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paste and order table</a> before refining valuable herbs. Stop when live Herblore reaches 70; no Mixology reward item is required.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-farming-70" number="28" title="Close only the remaining Farming gap to actual 70">
        <p>After a whole chapter of trees, fruit trees, Fossil hardwoods, herbs, Weiss and Farming Contracts, check the live skill tab. If it already reads <strong>actual 70</strong>, mark this complete without another run. Otherwise use the seeds and runs you prefer. For a bounded <em>active</em> catch-up rather than waiting several more real-world days, go to <strong>Tithe Farm in Hosidius</strong> with a seed dibber, spade and watering cans. Take the highest seeds your actual Farming permits (<strong>Bologano at 54</strong> until you qualify for a higher tier), plant, water and harvest in manageable batches, and repeat only until the measured XP gap closes. Tithe Farm is a fallback, not a mandatory minigame if passive Farming was enough. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tithe_Farm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Farm rules and seed tiers</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.6 exit · actual levels only</div>
        <h3>All eight Song of the Elves skills, without boosts.</h3>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Required actual level</th><th>Supplier / check</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Agility</td><td>70+</td><td>65 → Making Friends reward → final course</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Construction</td><td>70+</td><td>2.1 contracts + quest XP → Adept Homes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Farming</td><td>70+</td><td>Background runs; Tithe Farm if short</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Herblore</td><td>70+</td><td>Named lamps + live potion/Mixology XP</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hunter</td><td>70+</td><td>Eagles' Peak + Defender → rumours</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mining</td><td>70+</td><td>Actual 71 for the earlier stout strategy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Smithing</td><td>70+</td><td>Red Reef + Defender → live metal work</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Woodcutting</td><td>70+</td><td>Already actual 70 at Chapter 1 exit; no new grind</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <p><strong>Additional handoff:</strong> actual <strong>60 Ranged</strong> and Ava's accumulator; actual <strong>67 Sailing</strong> and a camphor-hulled skiff; full Fairytale II; Icthlarin's Little Helper, A Tail of Two Cats, Dream Mentor, Making Friends/Weiss, Eagles' Peak, What Lies Below, Defender of Varrock, The Red Reef and Making History complete. The relevant Tail/Fairytale/Defender/Making History lamps went to Herblore. No temporary boost counts toward this matrix.</p>
        <p><strong>2.7 owns the elf quests</strong>—Regicide → Roving Elves → Mourning's End Parts I/II → Song of the Elves—along with their inventory and boss preparation. Chapter 3 owns the actual-56 Slayer catch-up/Path of Glouphrie before While Guthix Sleeps, the deferred Curse of Arrav, and Sailing beyond 67. Do not add 2.7, Fishing 99, Agility 84/98, Smithing 74 or Slayer 56 here.</p>
      </section>

